Stop recording a staging hit's digest on the upload session (MEMNG-968 review r1).

The session then names no digest, the never-linked sweep's session clause matches nothing, and an
aged never-linked row is counted reclaimable and reclaimed while a session staged onto it through
POST /api/uploads is still open. The probe that must turn red is the route-level hold.

--- a/app/services/uploads.py
+++ b/app/services/uploads.py
@@ -525,7 +525,6 @@
         # with this digest and size, so the claim has been checked against stored bytes. It is what
         # holds that row against the never-linked sweep while this session is open (MEMNG-968). A
         # miss stores nothing — an unchecked claim must not read as a digest.
-        upload.sha256 = sha256
         await db.flush()
         return upload
     await to_thread.run_sync(_create_part_sync, part)
